          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Melville's Personal Struggles</strong><br>\nMelville faced professional obscurity and financial hardship in his later years. He struggled to gain the same acclaim he had enjoyed with his earlier works, and his last years were marked by personal and literary frustration.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Literary Style and Technique</strong><br>\nMelville is noted for his rich use of language and exploration of character psychology. He was adept at using allegory and narrative complexity to imbue his stories with depth and contemplative gravity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Melville's Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter his death in 1891, Melville's work was largely forgotten until a \"Melville Revival\" in the early 20th century. Today, he is considered one of America's greatest novelists, with \"Moby-Dick\" hailed as a masterpiece of world literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
